# Keep the development-only half of the repository out of the dist archive that
# Packagist serves. Without this a `composer require` downloads the test suite
# (3,089 tests and the CommonMark and GFM spec fixtures, 741 KiB of the 1.4 MiB
# tree) and this project's own CI, none of which the consumer can run: the only
# dev dependency is the test framework, and it is not installed.
#
# Measured with `git archive --format=zip`: 407,227 bytes down to 151,503, a 63%
# reduction. The entries below are the whole difference.
#
# What is *not* listed here ships, deliberately: `src/`, `bin/`, `composer.json`,
# `composer.lock`, `README.md` and `LICENSE`. The lock file stays because a
# reproducible install is worth 176 KiB, and `LICENSE` because the archive is
# redistributed under its terms.
/.github            export-ignore
/tests              export-ignore
/tools              export-ignore
/examples           export-ignore
/phpunit.xml.dist   export-ignore
/smoke.php          export-ignore
/stress.php         export-ignore
/readme-check.php   export-ignore
/sonar-project.properties export-ignore
